      "content": "Certainly, according to the Hazard Analysis Critical Control Point (HACCP) guidelines for poultry, you must cool the cooked meat from 54 degrees Celsius (130 degrees Fahrenheit) to 4 degrees Celsius (39.2 degrees Fahrenheit) within two hours, or to 60 degrees Fahrenheit or less (15.5 degrees Celsius) within four hours, to inhibit the growth of Clostridium perfringens. Ensuring that cooling logs accurately reflect these temperatures over the specified time frames is essential for compliance. Please go through your logs and confirm that these critical limits have been met.",
